2026-11-06 information-architecture.drawio (integrated flow)
Mistake: drew a separate screen for each app as a page and again as a side panel, and for its panels, so the same screen appeared over and over; gave regions slot names the renderer does not know, so every box was full width; left the story map and the story explorer inside the design canvas.
Correction: one screen per app, whether page or side panel; regions use the renderer's layouts (holy-grail, sidebar); the Story UI editor holds the map with a screen frames view, and the frames open a browser story explorer framed by design canvas screens.
2026-11-06 information-architecture.drawio (transition lines)
Mistake: the IA renderer drew a transition between screens in different columns as a straight orthogonal line, so on a row of screens every line ran through the screens between and the lines lay on top of each other.
Correction: drawio_ux.mjs routes each such line up from its own point on the source's top edge, along a lane of its own above every screen, and down into its own point on the target, so it crosses no screen or stories callout; specced in drawio_ux_map_spec.py.
